Package: tas2783-compat
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 alsa-ucm-conf
Recommends: firmware-misc-nonfree (>= 20260916)
Description: stop-gap fixes for TI TAS2783 SoundWire speakers
 Makes the internal speakers work on laptops with TI TAS2783 SoundWire
 amplifiers where the kernel, linux-firmware and alsa-ucm-conf do not
 agree yet:
 .
  * links the HP 8EA1 (OmniBook X Flip 14) amplifier firmware to the
    file names the tas2783-sdw driver requests;
  * adds the alsa-ucm-conf TAS2783 speaker profile, which is newer than
    the alsa-ucm-conf release in Debian;
  * turns off the WirePlumber "Pro Audio" profile on HP 8EA1, whose probe
    of the broken amplifier I/V-sense capture floods the kernel log.
 .
 The UCM profile is only linked in when alsa-ucm-conf does not provide
 it, so a newer alsa-ucm-conf takes over by itself.
